A tree seedling's height was recorded each week from week $2$ to week $9$, and a line of best fit was drawn.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, xscale=0.6, yscale=0.20]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(13,0);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,40);
\foreach \x in {0,2,4,6,8,10,12} {\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,0) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y in {5,10,15,20,25,30} {\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.3,\y) {$\y$};}
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.3,0) {$0$};
\foreach \p in {(2,10),(3,12),(4,14),(5,16),(6,19),(7,20),(8,22),(9,24)} {\fill \p circle (2.2pt);}
\draw[thick,blue] (2,10)--(9,24);
\draw[thick,blue,dashed] (0,6)--(2,10);
\draw[thick,blue,dashed] (9,24)--(12,30);
\node[rotate=90,font=\scriptsize] at (-1.8,20) {Height (cm)};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (6,-5) {Weeks since planting};
\node[font=\small] at (6,36) {Tree seedling height};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Use the line of best fit to predict the seedling's height at week $5$.

